; Class constructors and destructors: one of each per class or record,
; without parameters or directives, implemented (as `class constructor
; T.Name`, matching the declaration's name), static (no Self), and not
; members (they cannot be called; a method may have the same name), as in
; Free Pascal.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/classctor/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:5:23: error: only one class constructor can be declared in class 'T'
; CHECK: errors.pas:4:11: note: 'A' declared here
; CHECK: errors.pas:6:22: error: a class destructor cannot have parameters
; CHECK: errors.pas:11:22: error: 'virtual' cannot be used with a class destructor
; CHECK: errors.pas:17:20: error: a class destructor cannot have parameters
; CHECK: errors.pas:19:22: error: class 'T2' has no class constructor 'Wrong'
; CHECK: errors.pas:10:11: note: 'Init' declared here
; CHECK: errors.pas:20:33: error: use of undeclared identifier 'Self'
; CHECK: errors.pas:21:20: error: class 'T3' has no method 'Init'
; CHECK: errors.pas:10:23: error: class constructor 'T2.Init' is declared but never implemented
; CHECK: errors.pas:14:23: error: class constructor 'T3.Init' is declared but never implemented
; CHECK: errors.pas:23:6: error: no member named 'Init' in class 'T2'
; CHECK-NOT: error
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -c %S/Inputs/classctor/toplevel.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=TOP %s
; TOP: toplevel.pas:2:19: error: a class constructor must be declared in a class; implement it as 'class constructor TClass.X'
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/classctor/record.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=REC %s
; REC: record.pas:5:23: error: a class constructor cannot have parameters
; REC: record.pas:6:23: error: only one class constructor can be declared in record 'TR'
; REC: record.pas:5:11: note: 'Init' declared here
; REC: record.pas:8:22: error: a class constructor cannot have parameters
;
; The AST shows them as ClassConstructorDecl and ClassDestructorDecl.
; RUN: %p3 --mode=objfpc --emit-ast -o - %S/../run/classctor.pas | FileCheck --check-prefix=AST %s
; AST: ClassConstructorDecl 'tcounter.create' definition
; AST: ClassDestructorDecl 'tcounter.destroy' definition
; AST: ConstructorDecl 'tcounter.create' definition
